        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================



   Trion Bulkupload is an automated way to upload high numbers
   of files at a time with online one doscommand.

   Every file section has a directory where the fysical files are
   stored.
   When Bulkupload is started it will scan all files in these
   directories and check if they are present in the filecatalogue.
   If a file is not preset it will try to Add this file.

   Optionally you can let it process at single file section
   instead of all. Which is faster when only have added files
   to a single section.


   Bulkupload has a few options you can use on the command line:


Trion BulkUploader 1.08
Copyright (c)'96-'98, By Paul Spijkerman. All rights reserved.

Use:     TBulkUpload [-flags] [section] ["sysop"]
Section: if a number is used, only that section is processed.
Sysop:   if a name is used, that name will be used for Uploader.
Flags:   -D  ..  Use original date on file instead of now.
         -Q  ..  Quiet operation.
         -I  ..  Get Description file from archive.



   If you start with a name (between "") at the command line
   that name is used in the Uploader field if files are
   added to the filecatalogue. Default the name of
   the Bulkupload programm will be used.

   If you start with a number on the command line it will
   switch to "single section" mode .. and use the number
   for the file section number.

   If the -I flag is used the program wil use the upload script
   to process files and check if there is a description file
   like FILE_ID.DIZ present in archives .. and use it for
   the description of the file.

   If the -D flag is used the date from the file is used as
   the Upload date.. if you don't use this flag the time
   at the moment of adding the file is used as upload time.
   This flag is usefull if you build a filebase for the first
   time or remake the filebase .. so not all the files while
   be shown during a new file scan.

   This programm is very Usefull if you have to start a complete
   new file catalogue. Or if you lost your old file catalogue.

   Note that Bulkupload validates all files it uploads, so you
   don't have to validate them all bij hand or by CheckFileBase
   Utility.
